===Mergers===

*On [[February 3]], [[2003]], Shin'ichi from [[Ashina District, Hiroshima|Ashina District]] (dissolved by this action) merged into the expanded city of [[Fukuyama, Hiroshima|Fukuyama]].

*On [[March 1]], [[2003]], the town of [[Saeki, Hiroshima|Saeki]] and the village of [[Yoshiwa, Hiroshima|Yoshiwa]] from [[Saeki District, Hiroshima|Saeki District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Hatsukaichi, Hiroshima|Hatsukaichi]].

*On [[April 1]], [[2003]], the towns of [[Osaki, Hiroshima|Osaki]], [[Higashino, Hiroshima|Higashino]] and [[Kinoe, Hiroshima|Kinoe]] from [[Toyota District, Hiroshima|Toyota District]] merged to form the city of [[Osakikamijima, Hiroshima|Osakikamijima]].

*On [[April 1]], [[2003]], the town of [[Shimokamigari, Hiroshima|Shimokamigari]] from [[Aki District, Hiroshima|Aki District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Kure, Hiroshima|Kure]].

*On [[March 1]], [[2004]], K&amp;#333;ta, Midori, Mukaihara, Takamiya, Yachiyo, and Yoshida from [[Takata District, Hiroshima|Takata District]] (dissolved by this action) merged, creating the city of [[Akitakata, Hiroshima|Akitakata]].

*On [[April 1]], [[2004]], [[Funo, Hiroshima|Funo]], [[Kimita, Hiroshima|Kimita]], [[Kisa, Hiroshima|Kisa]],  [[Mirasaka, Hiroshima|Mirasaka]], [[Miwa, Hiroshima|Miwa]], and [[Sakugi, Hiroshima|Sakugi]] from [[Futami District, Hiroshima|Futami District]] (dissolved by this action) and [[Konu, Hiroshima|Konu]] from [[Konu District, Hiroshima|Konu District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Miyoshi, Hiroshima|Miyoshi]].

*On [[April 1]], [[2004]], the town of [[Joge, Hiroshima|Joge]] from [[Konu District, Hiroshima|Konu District]] merged with the expanded city of [[Fuchu, Hiroshima|Fuchu]].

*On [[April 1]], [[2004]], the town of [[Kawajiri, Hiroshima|Kawajiri]] from [[Toyota District, Hiroshima|Toyota Distrcit]] merged into the expanded city of [[Kure, Hiroshima|Kure]].

*On [[October 1]], [[2004]], the towns of [[Kozan, Hiroshima|Kozan]] and [[Seranishi, Hiroshima|Seranishi]] from [[Sera District, Hiroshima|Sera District]] merged into the expanded town of [[Sera, Hiroshima|Sera]].

*On [[October 1]], [[2004]], [[Kake, Hiroshima|Kake]], [[Togouchi, Hiroshima|Togouchi]], and [[Tsutsuga, Hiroshima|Tsutsuga]] from [[Yamagata District, Hiroshima|Yamagata District]] merged, creating the town of [[Akiota, Hiroshima|Akiota]].

*On [[November 1]], [[2004]], the town of Etajima from [[Aki District, Hiroshima|Aki District]] merged with the towns of [[Nomi, Hiroshima|Nomi]], [[Ogaki, Hiroshima|Ogaki]], and [[Okimi, Hiroshima|Okimi]] from [[Saeki District, Hiroshima|Saeki District]] forming the city of [[Etajima, Hiroshima|Etajima]].

*On [[November 5]], [[2004]], the towns of [[Jinseki, Hiroshima|Jinseki]], [[Sanwa, Hiroshima|Sanwa]], and [[Yuki, Hiroshima (Jinseki)|Yuki]] and the village of [[Toyomatsu, Hiroshima|Toyomatsu]] from [[Jinseki District, Hiroshima|Jinseki District]] merged, creating the town of [[Jinsekikogen, Hiroshima|Jinsekikogen]].

*On [[February 1]], [[2005]], [[Chiyoda, Hiroshima|Chiyoda]], [[Geihoku, Hiroshima|Geihoku]], [[Oasa, Hiroshima|Oasa]], and [[Toyohira, Hiroshima|Toyohira]] from [[Yamagata District, Hiroshima|Yamagata District]] merged, creating the town of [[Kitahiroshima, Hiroshima|Kitahiroshima]].

*On [[February 1]], [[2005]], [[Numakuma, Hiroshima|Numakuma]] from [[Numakuma District, Hiroshima|Numakuma District]] (dissolved by this action) merged with the expanded city of [[Fukuyama, Hiroshima|Fukuyama]].

*On [[February 7]], [[2005]],  [[Fukutomi, Hiroshima|Fukutomi]], [[Kochi, Hiroshima|Kochi]], [[Kurose, Hiroshima|Kurose]], and [[Toyosaka, Hiroshima|Toyosaka]] from [[Kamo District, Hiroshima|Kamo District]] and [[Akitsu, Hiroshima|Akitsu]] from [[Toyota District, Hiroshima|Toyota District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Higashihiroshima, Hiroshima|Higashihiroshima]].

*On [[March 20]], [[2005]], the towns of [[Ondo, Hiroshima|Ondo]], [[Kurahashi, Hiroshima|Kurahashi]], [[Kamagari, Hiroshima|Kamagari]] from [[Aki District, Hiroshima|Aki District]] and the towns of [[Yasuura, Hiroshima|Yasuura]], [[Toyohama, Hiroshima|Toyohama]] and [[Yutaka, Hiroshima|Yutaka]] from [[Toyota District, Hiroshima|Toyota District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Kure, Hiroshima|Kure]].

*On [[March 22]], [[2005]], the town of [[Daiwa, Hiroshima|Daiwa]] from the former [[Kamo District, Hiroshima|Kamo District]] (dissolved by this action), the town of [[Kui, Hiroshima|Kui]] from [[Mitsugi District, Hiroshima|Mitsugi District]], and the town of [[Hongo, Hiroshima|Hongo]] from [[Toyota District, Hiroshima|Toyota District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Mihara, Hiroshima|Mihara]].

*On [[March 28]], [[2005]], the towns of [[Mitsugi, Hiroshima|Mitsugi]] and [[Mukaishima, Hiroshima|Mukaishima]] from [[Mitsugi District, Hiroshima|Mitsugi District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Onomichi, Hiroshima|Onomichi]]. [[Mitsugi District, Hiroshima|Mitsugi District]] was dissolved as a result.

*On [[March 31]], [[2005]], the towns of [[Hiwa, Hiroshima|Hiwa]], [[Kuchiwa, Hiroshima|Kuchiwa]], [[Saijo, Hiroshima|Saijo]], [[Takano, Hiroshima|Takano]], and [[Tojo, Hiroshima|Tojo]], from the former [[Hiba District, Hiroshima|Hiba District]] (dissolved by this action) and the town of [[Souryo, Hiroshima|Souryo]] from the former [[Konu District, Hiroshima|Konu District]] (dissolved by this action) merged into the expanded city of [[Shobara, Hiroshima|Shobara]].

*On [[April 25]], [[2005]], the town of [[Yuki, Hiroshima|Yuki]] from [[Saeki District, Hiroshima|Saeki District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Hiroshima, Hiroshima|Hiroshima]].

*On [[November 3]], [[2005]], the towns of [[Miyajima, Hiroshima|Miyajima]] and [[Ono, Hiroshima|Ono]] from [[Saeki District, Hiroshima|Saeki District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Hatsukaichi, Hiroshima|Hatsukaichi]]. [[Saeki District, Hiroshima|Saeki District]] was dissolved as a result of this merger.

*On [[January 10]], [[2006]], the city of [[Innoshima, Hiroshima|Innoshima]] and the town of [[Setoda, Hiroshima|Setoda]] from [[Toyota District, Hiroshima|Toyota District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Onomichi, Hiroshima|Onomichi]].

*On March 1, 2006, the city of [[Kannabe, Hiroshima|Kannabe]] from [[Fukayasu District, Hiroshima|Fukayasu District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Fukuyama, Hiroshima|Fukuyama]]. [[Fukayasu District, Hiroshima|Fukayasu District]] was dissolved as a result of this merger.

== Economy ==
Hiroshima's main industries include automobiles ([[Mazda]] is headquartered in Hiroshima Prefecture) and shipbuilding ([[Kure, Hiroshima|Kure]] was one of the main naval bases of the [[Imperial Japanese Navy]] and remains a major commercial yard).

