      <minor />
      <comment>robot  Adding: ca</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">This is a '''list of the rulers of the [[Kingdom of Asturias]]'''.  While their existence and dates seem plausible, further verifiable details about their reigns are often scarce, especially for the early ones.

*[[Pelayo of Asturias|Pelayo]] ([[718]]–[[737]])
*[[Favila of Asturias|Favila]] ([[737]]–[[739]]), also spelled ''Favilac'' or ''Fáfila''
*[[Alfonso I of Asturias|Alfonso I]] ([[739]]–[[757]]), called ''the Catholic''
*[[Fruela I of Asturias|Fruela I]] ([[757]]–[[768]])
*[[Aurelio of Asturias|Aurelio]] ([[768]]–[[774]])
*[[Silo of Asturias|Silo]] ([[774]]–[[783]])
*[[Mauregato of Asturias|Mauregato the Usurper]] ([[783]]–[[788]])
*[[Bermudo I of Asturias|Bermudo I]] ([[788]]–[[791]]), also spelled ''Vermudo'' or ''Veremund'', called ''the Deacon''
*[[Alfonso II of Asturias|Alfonso II]] ([[791]]–[[842]]), called ''the Chaste''
*[[Ramiro I of Asturias|Ramiro I]] ([[842]]–[[850]])
*[[Ordoño I of Asturias|Ordoño I]] ([[850]]–[[866]])

During the reign of Ordoño I, the kingdom of Asturias progressively came to be known as the [[kingdom of León]]. The kingdom was split in [[910]] and Fruela received the part which kept the name of Asturias.

*[[Alfonso III of León|Alfonso III]] ([[866]]–[[910]]), called ''the Great''
*[[Fruela II of León|Fruela II]] ([[910]]–[[925]]), called ''the Cruel'', king of [[Kingdom of León|León]] and [[Kingdom of Galicia|Galicia]] from [[924]]

For the later kings, see the [[list of Leonese monarchs]] and the [[Kingdom of Galicia#Asturian Kings of Galicia|list of Galician monarchs]].

