      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Ordoño I''' ([[830]]?–[[May 27]], [[866]]), became king of [[Kingdom of Asturias|Asturias]] in [[850]].  In [[859]] he defeated [[Musa ibn Musa]] in a battle at [[Albelda]].

Ordoño was said to have directed the repopulation of the towns of [[León, León|León]], [[Astorga (Spain)|Astorga]], [[Tuy]], and [[Amaya]].

