      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Roman bridge near Covadonga Spain.jpg|thumb|200px|Roman Bridge]]
'''Cangas de Onís''' is a town in the eastern part of the province and autonomous community of [[Asturias]] in the northwest of [[Spain]]. Cangas de Onís was the ancient capital of the [[Kingdom of Asturias]].  It lies on the [[Sella River]], which is there spanned by a medieval &quot;Roman bridge&quot;. The population in [[1998]] was 6,211.

== External links ==
