      <contributor>
        <username>Arny</username>
        <id>479834</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>&quot;Dalmatian&quot; link updated</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''''The Hundred and One Dalmatians, or the Great Dog Robbery''''' is a [[1956]] novel by [[Dodie Smith]]. The plot revolves around a woman who steals 97 [[Dalmatian (dog)|dalmatian]] puppies in order to make a fur coat out of them. The protagonists of the novel are three adult dalmatians (Pongo and his wife Missis, and a young mother named Perdita) who set out to rescue their own fifteen puppies and wind up rescuing the whole lot. (The hundred-and-first dalmatian is part of a subplot unrelated to the puppy-snatching, and plays only a small part in the story.)

The novel was made into a [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]] [[animated film]] in [[1961]], under the title ''[[One Hundred and One Dalmatians]]''. In this film, and its live-action [[remake]] ''[[101 Dalmatians]]'', the four adult dalmatians were compressed into two, with two more anonymous puppies added to make up the numbers.

A sequel entitled '''The Starlight Barking''' follows on from the end of the first novel.

[[Category:1956 books|Hundred and One Dalmatians, The]]
[[Category:English novels|Hundred and One Dalmatians, The]]
[[Category:Fictional dogs|Hundred and One Dalmatians, The]]

[[de:101_Dalmatiner]]
{{Book-stub}}</text>
